<title>USA: Integon adopts shareholder rights plan.</title>
<headline>Integon adopts shareholder rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>WINSTON-SALEM, N.C. 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Integon Corp said on Wednesday that it adopted a shareholder rights plan to protect the company's stockholders from attempts to acquire control of Integon at an inadequate price.  </p>
<p>The company said that the rights plan was adopted &quot;in order to enhance the ability of the board to protect the interests of the company's stockholders.&quot;</p>
<p>Under the rights plan, a dividend distribution of one right would be made for each share of common stock outstanding at the close of business on February 11, 1997.</p>
<p>Each right entitles the holder to purchase one-thousandth of a share of a newly authorized series of Integon preferred stock at a purchase price of $70, it said.</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk 212 859-1611))</p>
